&lt;h4 style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cryptography Architect&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why We Have This Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Cryptography is the foundation that confidentiality, integrity, and trust in our systems rest on — and that foundation faces real pressure: weak or misused algorithms, poor key management, protocol vulnerabilities, and the looming migration to post-quantum cryptography. The Cryptography Architect leads the design and implementation of cryptographic frameworks that protect our systems and data —building resilience against these threats and earning our customers&#39; trust.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;How You’ll Find Success&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic Visionary: You hold a holistic view of the cryptographic threat landscape — from classical&amp;nbsp;attacks to the shift toward post-quantum cryptography — proactively identifying and mitigating&amp;nbsp;emerging risks. You guide cryptographic architecture strategy so it aligns with the organization’s risk&amp;nbsp;posture and business goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Innovator: Your drive for continuous improvement pushes you to explore and implement&amp;nbsp;cutting-edge cryptographic practices — post-quantum algorithms, key management modernization,&amp;nbsp;secure protocol design — keeping our systems resilient against evolving threats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative Leader: You build partnerships across security, engineering, and data science,&amp;nbsp;promoting best practices in cryptography. Your ability to foster collaboration creates an informed,&amp;nbsp;cohesive environment dedicated to protecting our systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resilient and Adaptive: You thrive in a fast-paced environment, managing complex projects while&amp;nbsp;guiding cross-functional teams through shifts in cryptographic standards or technology. Your&amp;nbsp;problem-solving skills are essential to navigating the complexities of cryptographic governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;How You’ll Grow&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape Industry Standards: Participate in industry conferences, standards bodies such as NIST and&amp;nbsp;IETF, and professional organizations to influence the future of cryptography and key management&amp;nbsp;practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive Presence: Increase your visibility and involvement in executive-level discussions, refining&amp;nbsp;how you communicate strategic security insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand Your Leadership Toolkit: As a thought leader in cryptography architecture, mentor and&amp;nbsp;coach emerging talent, growing the cryptographic expertise across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complex Problem-Solving: Tackle significant cryptography challenges that sharpen your analytical,&amp;nbsp;critical thinking, and strategic planning abilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Things You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive Innovation in Cryptography: Lead research, evaluation, and implementation of next-generation cryptographic technologies and methodologies — post-quantum algorithms, modern key&amp;nbsp;management, secure protocol design — that support our products and platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct Security Reviews: Perform security reviews of cryptographic implementations and&amp;nbsp;proposed designs, including key management systems, protocols, and cryptographic integrations&amp;nbsp;across products, identifying risks such as weak or deprecated algorithms, improper key handling,&amp;nbsp;and protocol vulnerabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Key Management Architecture: Own the strategy and architecture for key management across&amp;nbsp;the organization — key generation, distribution, rotation, escrow, and destruction — including&amp;nbsp;KMS/HSM integration, envelope encryption, and secrets management, ensuring the full key lifecycle&amp;nbsp;is designed and operated to withstand compromise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop Standards &amp;amp; Reference Architectures: Author cryptography-related technical security&amp;nbsp;standards, guardrails, and reference architectures — encryption standards, key management&amp;nbsp;standards, PKI architecture — grounded in industry-wide frameworks such as NIST SP 800-57, FIPS&amp;nbsp;140-3, and NIST’s post-quantum cryptography standards, giving product and engineering teams a&amp;nbsp;secure, repeatable blueprint for building and deploying cryptographic solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape Security Strategy: Develop a comprehensive cryptography strategy that aligns with the&amp;nbsp;organization’s risk profile and business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage Complex Projects: Oversee execution of large-scale cryptography initiatives — such as PKI&amp;nbsp;modernization or post-quantum migration — ensuring on-time, on-budget delivery while proactively&amp;nbsp;addressing risks and fostering adaptability within teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a Culture of Excellence: Create an environment that promotes knowledge sharing,&amp;nbsp;collaboration, and continuous learning. Mentor colleagues to build a high-performing team&amp;nbsp;committed to our security objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For On Your Resume&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;While we value the wealth of experience, we put more emphasis on your capability and the outcomes&amp;nbsp;you’ve produced. For this role, these elements are particularly important:
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive Architectural Expertise: 5+ years of experience in cryptography, security architecture, or a&amp;nbsp;related field, with a proven history of designing secure cryptographic architectures; capable of&amp;nbsp;leading strategic initiatives to strengthen security posture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Expertise: Strong understanding of cryptographic primitives and protocols — symmetric&amp;nbsp;and asymmetric encryption, hashing, digital signatures, TLS/PKI. Deep, hands-on knowledge of key&amp;nbsp;management (generation, rotation, escrow, destruction, KMS/HSM integration) and fluency in&amp;nbsp;industry-wide standards and frameworks, including NIST SP 800-57, FIPS 140-2/140-3, and NIST’s&amp;nbsp;post-quantum cryptography standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated Initiative Leadership: Proven experience leading large-scale cryptography initiatives,&amp;nbsp;coordinating cross-functional teams to align with security guidelines while driving operational&amp;nbsp;efficiency and business growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic Mindset: Ability to translate cryptography challenges into actionable solutions that&amp;nbsp;integrate with business objectives and risk management frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaboration &amp;amp; Communication Skills: Excellent communication abilities to engage effectively with&amp;nbsp;both technical and non-technical stakeholders, fostering constructive partnerships across the&amp;nbsp;organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;What You Should Know About This Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our teams emphasizes technical craftsmanship, collaboration across languages and domains, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ll join a culture committed to innovation, mentorship, and shared ownership with a strong focus on quality and reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We partner closely with product, infrastructure, and data science teams to solve challenging problems at large scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunities to lead initiatives that influence company technical strategy and operational maturity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
