&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Federal Health Enterprise Account Executive&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why We Have This Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;The Qualtrics Federal sales team is a group of highly driven individuals dedicated to closing experience gaps across U.S. Federal organizations. The Fed Health Enterprise Account Executive is expected to serve as the person to pursue all sales efforts within the assigned territory, including prospect identification, lead generation, solution calls, advancing the sales cycle, proposal development, contract negotiation, forecasting, and deal closure. The focus is on driving incremental revenue for Federal product lines and buyer personas. As a Federal Enterprise Account Executive, your overarching objective is to drive company revenue growth through net new customer acquisition and strategic expansion across the current customer base within Fed Health - HHS.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How You’ll Find Success&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mission Alignment: Takes the initiative to understand the HHS mission of serving veterans and their families, create a strategic plan, and execute.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relationship Elevation: Elevates customer relationships to the next level through dedicated account management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process Discipline: Experience using enterprise sales processes such as MEDDICC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solution Expertise: Ability to learn and understand product solutions and features with excellent verbal and written communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical Mindset: Strong quantitative, analytical, and conflict resolution abilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Presence: Willingness to travel and be client-facing 50% of the time (approximate travel time dependent on team and to be confirmed by Hiring Manager).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Location: Based out of the Washington D.C., Maryland, Northern-Virginia (DMV) area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How You’ll Grow&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;With a mission-first approach, the Qualtrics Federal team helps some of the largest and most impactful U.S. Federal organizations listen, understand, and take action on customer data.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;You will sell technology to solve real agency problems and tackle challenges that directly impact the health outcomes and experiences of U.S. veterans.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;If you love a strategic, analytical sales process and working across diverse stakeholders in the Federal healthcare space, selling Qualtrics software will always keep you learning and growing.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Things You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate: &amp;nbsp;Lead the HHS deal team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategize: Develop a territory plan and specific account plans to drive usage of the Qualtrics platform across Fed Health and its administrations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise: Become a trusted advisor to a variety of buyers in the Federal Healthcare vertical.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute: Closely engage with clients at all points of the sales cycle—from prospecting, product demonstrations, and onsite presentations to contracting and closing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand: Drive net new revenue growth through new logo acquisition and expansion of current accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform: Meet quarterly and annual sales targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate: Be a thought leader and customer advocate with partners to elevate the adoption of experience management (XM).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner: Work closely with Qualtrics ecosystem resources and partners to identify and develop new strategic opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For On Your Resume&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience specifically managing accounts or selling into the Healthcare/HHS space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successful track record of achieving assigned targets within the Federal vertical.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successful track record providing executive-level impact to clients and partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Well-versed in Federal procurement processes and regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Well-versed in Federal government security standards and policies (FedRAMP, HIPAA, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in building relationships with relevant Federal Healthcare contractors and GSIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience responding to and winning competitive RFx solicitations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing relationships within the HHS territory (VHA, VBA, NCA) preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Should Know About This Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Qualtrics Federal team prides itself on a strong culture of collaboration, hard-working mentality, and commitment to winning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualtrics Federal is the fastest-growing market unit within the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are just getting started. Join a team that is defining the Experience Management category in the Federal space and making a difference for our customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Team’s Favorite Perks and Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quarterly in-person team activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Federal-specific training and focused sales enablement sessions to support individual success and career growth.&lt;/li&gt;
